							author: "Crypt1c"
							filtered_title: "Black Holes"
							pages: [
								"{\"text\":\"       Black Holes\\n\\n- Holes in space-time\\n- Dangerous but useful?\\n- Condense high-matter objects into a small space\\n- Alchemical clay is not enough\\n- Singularity-based ones are too small\\n- I can calc the radius and life of bh?\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"       Black Holes\\n\\n- Schwarzschild Radius formula:\\nr = (M*G/c^2)*2\\n  r: Radius\\n  M: Mass of the object\\n  G: Gravitational Constant = 6.67430×10^−11N^m2 kg^−2\\n  c: Speed of Light = 2.99×10^8 m/s\\n\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"       Black Holes\\n\\n- Hawking Radiation Formula:\\nt = (M/Mo)^3* 1.160x10^67 yr\\n\\n  t: BH Lifetime\\n  M: Mass of BH\\n  Mo: 1 solar mass = 1.989x10^30\"}"
								"{\"extra\":[{\"italic\":true,\"text\":\" The page is covered    in various drawings      and magic circles\"}],\"text\":\"       Black Holes\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"       Black Holes\\n\\n- Infinity based bh (I-BH) last much longer than singularity based ones, even with the same mass\\n- I think the neutronium casing is reflecting some of the radiation back?\\n- It's definetly the neutronium\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"       Black Holes\\n\\nI-BH Hawking Radiation Formula:\\nt = (M/Mo)^3 * e^n 1.160x10^67 yr\\n\\n  t: BH Lifetime\\n  M: Mass of BH\\n  Mo: 1 solar mass = 1.989x10^30\\n  n: Neutronium Decay-Prevetntion Rate: 24*# Infinity\"}"
								"{\"extra\":[{\"bold\":true,\"text\":\"required\"},{\"text\":\" to stabilize the bh or else it self implodes really quickly\\n- Explosion from I-BH isn't as big as I expected, but it can chip away at the bounds of reality. Could be useful in future fights. \"}],\"text\":\"       Black Holes\\n\\n- **Magic is \"}"
